From 79542ac1e9fd1f520932fa178891fa68ace1b511 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:48:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(session): drop assistant messages with no provider
 content (empty-assistant-guard)

Strict providers (Kimi) reject assistant messages with no content with
400 "must not be empty", permanently wedging the session: every retry
persists another error husk and the session can never send again.

- Emit an assistant message only when it contributes provider content:
  non-empty text, a tool call, non-empty reasoning, or same-model
  reasoning carrying a replayable signed/redacted payload (Anthropic
  signed-thinking replay preserved; dropped after a model switch).
- Drop empty step-split blocks before conversion so a non-empty sibling
  step can no longer ship an empty assistant turn.
- Guard tolerates undefined text (no .trim() crash).

Tests: message-v2.fix5.test.ts (11 cases) + existing suite 39/39.
Upstream: anomalyco/opencode#53571 (PR #53575).
